From e148edd179debf86035510ed147732ef192e9ca0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:52:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(sim): judge a tool body by the band stack the
 simulation draws

Law (c) shank/holder reach, the (c3) mid-turn sweep and every law that
reads verify::Cutter (solid b2, containment solid, posed rapids, rotary
field) now read a modelled body's band stack - the shape the fixture
laws sweep and the simulation draws - instead of the single cylinder
enclosing it. The bands ride on the cutter (Cutter::body, a fixed-
capacity BodyBands), refused back to the cylinder when they do not fit
the judged record; a tool with no body reads bit-identically. Law (c)
reports a move once per group (shank, then holder or body bands).

The drill-reach, cross-drill and probe stylus laws keep the enclosing
cylinder and now say so by name (operation::body_judged); moving them
is #842.

Fixes #835

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
